     "type": "text",
     "value": "All theses must have an abstract. The abstract provides readers with a general opinion about the thesis. In the first paragraph of this section, the subject of the thesis must be explained. In other paragraphs, the scope and purposes of the performed study must be explained individually, utilized methods must be mentioned briefly, and the main conclusions must be included as well. The abstract of Master theses must be at least 150 words, and must not exceed 350 words. It should not extend to the second page. Doctoral theses do not have word limit. Both Master and Doctoral theses must have Five (5) Keywords in English. Abstract page is paginated as “iv”. Initial letters of keywords must be capitalized. This is an abstract. It must be a maximum of 350 words. It should not extend to the second page.",
